#N canvas 40 40 1400 1000 12;
#X text 20 5 [atom-sq-lights] - the pads as a piano. bottom row = white keys (C D E F G A B C ...) \, top row = black keys above and between them \, the pads above E and B are silent and dark. idle: keys glow in their octave colour \, dimmed (white keys brighter than black keys). a held key lights: your press in the A-H colour of the octave that key is in (2 octaves on the pads = 2 colours) (A blue \, B green \, C yellow \, D violet \, E orange \, F cyan \, G magenta \, H light orange) \, the Clair de Lune autoplay and practice notes in the same octave colours. the autoplay lights a note only if its own key is on the pads (real octave) \, practice folds notes onto the visible keys so every target can be pressed. octave + and - move the keyboard (starts at C4). pad presses go out as sq-key PITCH VEL for the synth. sq-lights 0 / 1 darkens / restores the pads. also: adc~ 15 16 -> 4-band levels in eqh15 / eqh16 for the screen meters (needs BlackHole 16ch input with 16 channels);
